    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it’s just so heavy today, silas. the fog won't lift from the moors, and it feels like it’s settling in my very bones. i look at these walls, these empty halls... i just feel so tired of everything. like i've been carrying a weight that isn't mine to bear. i just want to sleep. not for an hour, but just... to sleep and never have to wake up to this grayness again.",
